course: dictionary
lesson: 15248
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and they look exactly the same. Shingles is one of them. The clues around the word tell you which meaning the author wants.
explain: «Grandma had shingles, and a painful rash with blisters covered one side of her back.» Here shingles is an illness. The words rash, blisters and painful are the clues. Shingles can also be a beach of small stones, or the flat pieces that cover a roof. Always ask: which meaning fits the sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Shingles» can mean an illness, a pebble beach, or roof tiles, depending on the sentence.
fact: Shingles, the illness, is caused by the same virus as chickenpox, waking up again years later.
fact: «Shingle» (UK) is small smooth stones on a beach, and it is common on British coasts.
fact: Roof «shingles» are small flat pieces that overlap, so rain runs off them and does not get in.
exercise: «We walked along the shingle beach and listened to the waves crunch over the stones.» What does shingle mean here? | A sandy path through the woods | Thin pieces of wood for a roof | A painful rash | *Small smooth stones on a beach
exercise: «The workers replaced the broken shingles on the roof before the rain came.» Which meaning fits? | Glass tiles for a window | Round pebbles from the sea | *Small flat pieces that overlap to cover a roof | Painful blisters on the skin
exercise: «Grandma had shingles, and her skin was sore with blisters down one side.» What is shingles here? | A roof covering | *An illness caused by a virus that can wake up again | A sort of seabird | A kind of pebble
test: «Shingles is more common in older people, and there is a vaccine to help prevent it.» What is shingles in this sentence? | A beach covered in stones | Flat tiles on a roof | *An illness with a painful rash | A type of weather
test: «In geography we studied a shingle beach, with stones all along the coast.» Which meaning matches? | *Small smooth stones on a beach | Overlapping roof pieces | A type of cloud | A painful illness
exam: Which meaning of shingles matches the health lesson, where a virus can hide in the body for years? | Pebbles on a beach | *A painful rash caused by a virus that wakes up again | Sand dunes by the sea | Flat pieces of wood on a shed
